From: Andrew LaMarche <andrewjlamarche@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Feb 2026 01:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] uboot-mediatek: add support for BananaPi BPi-R4 Pro 8X

The BPi R4 Pro 8X can boot from microSD, SPI-NAND and eMMC. Add the board
definitions required for each storage option.

Adapted for the OpenWrt main M01 through M04 migration:
- keep R4 Pro common data separate from the 8X model;
- use the accepted upstream board and FIT configuration names;
- implement read-only SD production and recovery boot in M02;
- initialize and persist the complete SD environment in M04 so the
  randomly generated MAC address survives reboot;
- keep eMMC and SPI-NAND environments as explicit deferred markers; and
- exclude TFTP, installation, system-image writes, and onboard-storage flows.

Original-OpenWrt-Commit: 2f225358194cd56b2d29d9e97d0271490fb5f807
Original-Patch: package/boot/uboot-mediatek/patches/472-add-bpi-r4-pro-8x.patch
Source: OpenWrt PR #21083
Co-authored-by: Frank Wunderlich <frank-w@public-files.de>
Signed-off-by: Andrew LaMarche <andrewjlamarche@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-emmc.dts b/arch/arm/dts/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-emmc.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4d427facad3c714381e970bdd2eacc696e044f9d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-emmc.dts
